"modification": "Esterification of the Phenolic Hydroxyl",
"rationale": "The phenolic hydroxyl group on the indole ring is likely participating in hydrogen bonding, but it could also be a source of metabolic instability via glucuronidation or sulfation. Esterification with a simple methyl group (as shown) would block this metabolic liability while potentially improving membrane permeability. While the hydrogen bond donor is lost, the increased lipophilicity could improve binding affinity by promoting hydrophobic interactions within the HDAC1 active site. This is a common strategy to improve drug-like properties and bioavailability. The methyl ester is also synthetically accessible via reaction with diazomethane or methyl iodide under basic conditions."
