"modification": "Introduction of a Methyl Group at the Phenolic Hydroxyl",
"rationale": "Similar to the previous modification, this introduces a methyl group to the phenolic hydroxyl. However, this modification introduces a chiral center, which could lead to diastereomeric selectivity in binding. While this is a risk, it also presents an opportunity. If one diastereomer binds significantly better, it could lead to a substantial potency increase. The synthesis would involve a stereoselective methylation of the phenol, which could be challenging but is not impossible.  The increased lipophilicity would also be beneficial, as in the previous suggestion.",
