"modification": "Replacement of the Ester Linkage with an Amide",
"rationale": "The ester linkage is susceptible to enzymatic hydrolysis *in vivo*. Replacing it with an amide would significantly improve metabolic stability.  Amides are generally more resistant to hydrolysis than esters.  The amide nitrogen can also act as a hydrogen bond acceptor, potentially forming a favorable interaction with the HDAC1 active site.  The synthesis would involve reacting the carboxylic acid with methylamine using standard peptide coupling conditions.",
